  <static seed="1881" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionApplication/FractionSubtractionWordProblems10.pg">
    <statement><p>A trail<rsq/>s total length is <m>{{\frac{4}{15}}}</m> of a mile. It has two legs. The first leg is <m>{{\frac{1}{10}}}</m> of a mile long. How long is the second leg?</p>
<p>The second leg is <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/> of a mile in length.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{1}{6}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>This is a subtraction problem.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}[t]
   {{\frac{4}{15}}} - {{\frac{1}{10}}} 
      \amp = \frac{4 \cdot 2}{15 \cdot 2}-\frac{1 \cdot 3}{10 \cdot 3} \\
      \amp = \frac{8}{30} - \frac{3}{30} \\
      \amp = \frac{8-3}{30} \\
      \amp = \frac{5}{30} \\
      \amp = {{\frac{1}{6}}}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>The second leg is <m>{{\frac{1}{6}}}</m> of a mile in length.</p>
</solution>
